From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:20:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: synopsys: dw-dp: Detect the sink again on HPD
 IRQs when it was not found

With out-of-band HPD (USB-C DP Alt Mode), a DisplayPort sink that was
hung or still powering up when HPD went high is never detected: the
detect() call that follows the HPD rising edge cannot read the DPCD,
reports the connector as disconnected and nothing tries again. HPD
stays high (the dock keeps it asserted and sends Attention messages
with IRQ_HPD), so there is no further plug edge, and the short pulse
path in dw_dp_hpd_work() only checks the link status of an enabled
link, which there isn't. Power cycling the hung monitor leaves DP-1
disconnected until the cable is replugged.

Remember whether the last detect() found a sink, and treat a short
pulse as a hotplug event when it did not, so that the connector is
probed again (DPCD, EDID) and userspace is notified once the sink
answers. Do the same when a branch device reports a change of its
downstream ports (DP_DOWNSTREAM_PORT_STATUS_CHANGED), which is how a
DP-to-HDMI converter signals that its monitor was power cycled while
HPD stays high. Also warn (rate limited) when HPD is high but the sink
does not answer on AUX, which was silent so far.

Reproducer (Orange Pi 5, USB-C dock, Dell P2415Q on DP pin
assignment D): hang or power off the monitor, then power it on again.
Before, DP-1 stays "disconnected" with DP Alt Mode active and hpd=1
while the dock sends Attention/IRQ_HPD every ~2 s; after, the next
IRQ_HPD re-runs detection and DP-1 comes back.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
index 5b7490a2a01d..dfc17d4a87ad 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
@@ -364,6 +364,8 @@ struct dw_dp {
 	u8 pixel_mode;
 	bool usbc_mode;
 	bool usbc_hpd;
+	/* the last detect() found a sink answering on AUX */
+	bool sink_detected;
 	bool pm_active;
 
 	struct drm_bridge *next_bridge;
@@ -2097,11 +2099,18 @@ static enum drm_connector_status dw_dp_bridge_detect(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	if (PM_RUNTIME_ACQUIRE_ERR(&pm))
 		return connector_status_disconnected;
 
+	WRITE_ONCE(dp->sink_detected, false);
+
 	if (!dw_dp_hpd_detect(dp))
 		return connector_status_disconnected;
 
-	if (!dw_dp_hpd_detect_link(dp, connector))
+	if (!dw_dp_hpd_detect_link(dp, connector)) {
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(dp->dev,
+				     "HPD is high, but the sink does not respond on AUX\n");
 		return connector_status_disconnected;
+	}
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(dp->sink_detected, true);
 
 	return connector_status_connected;
 }
@@ -2387,6 +2396,21 @@ static int dw_dp_link_retrain(struct dw_dp *dp)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* A branch device signals changes on its downstream ports with IRQ_HPD */
+static bool dw_dp_downstream_port_changed(struct dw_dp *dp)
+{
+	u8 status;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* AUX goes through the PHY, which is off while the link is disabled */
+	if (phy_power_on(dp->phy))
+		return false;
+	ret = drm_dp_dpcd_readb(&dp->aux, DP_LANE_ALIGN_STATUS_UPDATED, &status);
+	phy_power_off(dp->phy);
+
+	return ret == 1 && (status & DP_DOWNSTREAM_PORT_STATUS_CHANGED);
+}
+
 static void dw_dp_hpd_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct dw_dp *dp = container_of(work, struct dw_dp, hpd_work);
@@ -2404,6 +2428,20 @@ static void dw_dp_hpd_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	dev_dbg(dp->dev, "[drm] Get hpd irq - %s\n", long_hpd ? "long" : "short");
 
+	/*
+	 * A short pulse (IRQ_HPD, or a DP Alt Mode Attention with HPD still
+	 * high) is only a link status check if the sink was detected. If the
+	 * last detection failed while HPD was high, e.g. because the sink was
+	 * hung or still powering up and did not answer on AUX, nothing else
+	 * would ever detect it again, as HPD does not go low: treat the pulse
+	 * as a hotplug event. The same applies when a branch device reports a
+	 * change on its downstream port (a DP-to-HDMI converter whose monitor
+	 * was power cycled).
+	 */
+	if (!long_hpd && (!READ_ONCE(dp->sink_detected) ||
+			  dw_dp_downstream_port_changed(dp)))
+		long_hpd = true;
+
 	if (!long_hpd) {
 		if (dw_dp_needs_link_retrain(dp)) {
 			ret = dw_dp_link_retrain(dp);
